A. Correlation of verifier misses (one-factor probit; r = latent correlation)
   Panko 1999 spreadsheet triads, pooled (individual miss 0.37; triad miss 0.17)    independent 0.051  observed 0.170  ->  r = 0.60
      same, nominal-group estimate (triad miss 0.19)                                independent 0.051  observed 0.190  ->  r = 0.68
   Mammography pairing (single miss ~0.20; pair miss ~0.12, low end of gain)        independent 0.040  observed 0.120  ->  r = 0.75
      same, high end of gain (pair miss ~0.08)                                      independent 0.040  observed 0.080  ->  r = 0.44
   Ulery 2012 same examiner retest (FN 0.075; 30% of FNs repeat)                    independent 0.006  observed 0.022  ->  r = 0.52
   Joint miss of k independent readers at f = 0.40 (imitator-style errors, thread S centre):
     r = 0.00  k=1: 0.400  k=2: 0.160  k=3: 0.064  k=5: 0.010
     r = 0.30  k=1: 0.400  k=2: 0.206  k=3: 0.122  k=5: 0.055
     r = 0.50  k=1: 0.400  k=2: 0.239  k=3: 0.167  k=5: 0.102
     r = 0.65  k=1: 0.400  k=2: 0.267  k=3: 0.206  k=5: 0.147
   So the second reader removes about a third of the remaining misses at r = 0.5,
   not 60% as independence would say, and the fifth reader adds little.

