C. Decomposed verification: a cone with m invalid entries, each checked locally
   per-entry miss f_e; same verifier for all entries (person factor shared, lam_p = 0.30)
   against a different verifier per entry (common factor only, lam_c = 0.20)
   f_e = 0.15  m=1: same 0.151, different 0.150, indep 0.150 | m=2: same 0.057, different 0.035, indep 0.022 | m=3: same 0.031, different 0.010, indep 0.003
   f_e = 0.25  m=1: same 0.250, different 0.250, indep 0.250 | m=2: same 0.119, different 0.084, indep 0.062 | m=3: same 0.073, different 0.034, indep 0.016
   f_e = 0.35  m=1: same 0.350, different 0.351, indep 0.350 | m=2: same 0.197, different 0.150, indep 0.122 | m=3: same 0.132, different 0.074, indep 0.043
   A single plausible slip (m = 1) gets no compounding: f_cone = f_e. The gain from
   decomposition is the lower local f_e and the location of the error (one task query).
   False flags on a correct cone of c entries, per-entry false-flag rate e; an adjudicator
   (a second referee shown the flag) upholds a spurious flag with probability 0.25:
     e = 0.002  c=30: 0.06 -> 0.01  c=100: 0.18 -> 0.05  c=300: 0.45 -> 0.14
     e = 0.005  c=30: 0.14 -> 0.04  c=100: 0.39 -> 0.12  c=300: 0.78 -> 0.31
     e = 0.010  c=30: 0.26 -> 0.07  c=100: 0.63 -> 0.22  c=300: 0.95 -> 0.53
   Without adjudication (or route (i) with excusal), large cones are rarely accepted.

D. P(works): output failure <= 5% and effort <= a fifth of chained imitation's
   F = (p*w*rbar + h)*f_V; p~U[.1,.5], rbar~U[1,1.6], u~logN(0,.55); h = 0 here (the folder
   conditions on the human's own chain succeeding; h > 0 is reported at the end);
   T/K log-uniform on [3,30]; beta = 1 audit per output; a located rejection of a correct
   result costs 1.05 steps, an unlocated one a full scan of n = 1.5 n0 steps.
   Calibration against verified-slack.md (its f ranges; spread over the range by u):
     math       V-human, f in [0.2, 0.5]                   model 39% (output 60%, effort 74%)  folder 40%
     math       V-cone, f in [0.1, 0.35], typed entries    model 40% (output 81%, effort 81%)  folder 45%
